INT. ABANDONED LIGHTHOUSE LENS ROOM, MOONLIGHT - NIGHT

A great Fresnel lens, dark, towering over the room like a cathedral of cut glass. A rusted catwalk wraps it. Wind sings through broken panes.

Four people sit on crates in a loose circle, sharing a thermos. They are strangers by temperament, partners by accident.

CALLISTA ROUSSEL-OKAFOR (30s, field jacket, a laptop open on her knee) taps keys. DESMOND "DES" ACHTERBERG-NNAMDI (40s, bearded, binoculars at his chest) glasses the sea. MARIGOLD PEMBERTON-ASANTE (50s, silver hair, birdwatcher's vest) tends the thermos. And young ZEPHYR KOWALCZYK-ADEYEMI (20s, headphones at his neck, restless) paces the catwalk.

The sea beyond is flat as slate. The moon is a coin on it.

MARIGOLD
(to the group)
Tea, anyone?

DES
Please.

CALLISTA
Not now.

ZEPHYR
(from above)
Nothing yet.

MARIGOLD
(muttering)
Always nothing yet, then everything at once.

She pours. The steam rises in a thin ribbon. Callista types. Des lowers the binoculars.

DES
(to Callista)
You're sure of the coordinates?

CALLISTA
I'm sure of the data. Whoever sent it, less so.

DES
(to himself)
It's a wild goose chase.

ZEPHYR
(calling down)
It's a boat.

They all look up. Zephyr points. On the black water, a light, small and white, is moving toward the lighthouse.

CALLISTA
That's not on the schedule.

DES
No lights, then lights.

MARIGOLD
Hush. Let it come.

The boat grows. A slow engine. Zephyr descends the catwalk with quick steps. The four of them gather at the window. Wind whines in the glass.

The boat slides up to the rocks. A figure climbs onto the landing. Thin, soaked, a case in one hand. He is already climbing the iron stair.

INSPECTOR MALACHI QUARTERMAINE-OSEI (50s, long coat, hat in hand) steps into the lens room, and stops. He looks at each of them in turn.

MALACHI
Good evening. Thank you for waiting.

Callista closes her laptop. Slowly. Des lowers his binoculars. Marigold sets down the thermos. Zephyr moves, quietly, between the inspector and the stair.

MALACHI (CONT'D)
(mildly)
Please. Don't. I'm here as a friend.

He sets the case on a crate and opens it. Inside, a folded sheet of paper and a revolver.

MALACHI (CONT'D)
One of you wrote to me. I should like to know which.

Silence. The moon cuts through the lens and throws one blade of light across the floor.
